-- title:
--   Openness of the uniformised locus after nilpotent base change
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ (a domain) with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal and every element satisfies, modulo that ideal, a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$. Let $G$ be a type and let $f_M : M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be a scheme locally of finite type. Let $\Theta_f$ assign, to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$, a map from $\bigl(\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O\text{-alg}}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},B)\times \Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B)\bigr)\times G$ to the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$; here $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B)$ is the set of Deligne data over $B$, that is, families of $B$-submodules $\mathrm{line}(L)\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}L$ indexed by the full $\mathcal O$-lattices $L$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, compatible with inclusions of lattices and with homotheties, and satisfying the stated nondegeneracy condition at each prime of $B$. Assume $\Theta_f$ is natural in $B$ (hypothesis `hnat`) and formally étale in the sense of `het`: for every surjection $p : B \to B_0$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent in both and with square-zero kernel, every $x_0$ over $B_0$ and every $B$-point $y$ of $M$ with $p_*y = \Theta_f(x_0)$ admit a unique $x$ over $B$ lifting $x_0$ with $\Theta_f(x)=y$. Let $C$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to C$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and let $p_1 : N \to M$, $p_2 : N \to \operatorname{Spec} C$ form a cartesian square over $f_M$ and $\operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Then there is an open subset $W$ of the underlying space of $N$ consisting exactly of those $n$ for which there exist a field $k$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent in $k$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi : C \to k$, and a morphism $z : \operatorname{Spec} k \to N$ with $z$ followed by $p_2$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ and with $z$ carrying the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ to $n$, together with a Deligne datum $P$ over $k$ and $g \in G$ such that the morphism underlying $\Theta_f\bigl((\varphi\circ\psi, P), g\bigr)$ equals $z$ followed by $p_1$.
--
--   This is the openness of the locus uniformised by Drinfeld's formal upper half plane, for a formally étale uniformisation map $\Theta_f$ into a scheme locally of finite type over $\mathcal O$, tested after base change to an $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ carrying a coefficient map from $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_isOpen_inter_eq_image_of_formallyEtale`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_isOpen_inter_eq_image_of_formallyEtale) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_isOpen_forall_mem_and_iff_exists_uniformization_of_locallyOfFiniteType`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_isOpen_forall_mem_and_iff_exists_uniformization_of_locallyOfFiniteType) in the treatment of Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of Shimura curves.
